[E0314] Error: `Point` cannot be passed to or from C
    ╭─[ err/26_extern_types/main.wip:13:16 ]
    │
 13 │     fn draw(p: Point)
    │                ──┬──
    │                  ╰──── not a C-compatible type
    │
    │ Note: extern functions can take and return only integers of up to 64 bits, `f32`, `f64`, `bool`, `cstring`, `ptr<T>` and C's structs; a parameter may also be a `str` or a `&[T]`, which pass as a pointer and a length, an array by reference, which passes as a pointer to its first element, or a function that takes and answers no struct by value, and no function that may be null, and whose own types cross, which passes as a C function pointer; a result may be `never`, for a C function that does not return
────╯
